  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "What is $9%$ of $1,000?$",
  "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $1,000$, and the percentage is $9%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n9%=9÷100=0.09\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =9%\\times 1,000 \\\\  & =0.09\\times 1,000 \\\\  & =90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $9%$ of $1,000$ is $90.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n9%=\\frac{9}{100}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =9%\\times 1,000 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{100}\\times 1,000 \\\\  & =9\\times \\frac{1,000}{100} \\\\  & =9\\times 10 \\\\  & =90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $9%$ of $1,000$ is $90.$",
